          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em dependent product
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal construction
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            to the situation where the codomain may
            %em depend
            on the domain, and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalizes
            indexed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            concept is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            makes sense for any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+sets"} family of sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            makes sense for any family of objects. In each case, however, the family is indexed by a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
          %p
            First we need to describe a family of objects indexed by an object; it's common to interpret this as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: E \to A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            would be the index set of the family, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of the bundle over an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            would be the set indexed by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            can be constructed as its
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
          %p
            In these terms, the cartesian product of the family of sets is the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of (global)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ev
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev: S \times A \to E
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi ev
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi π
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times A \stackrel{ev}\to E \stackrel{\pi}\to A
          %p
            equals the usual product projection from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times A
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ev
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            are both morphisms in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is that, given any set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            and morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \times A \to E
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \to S
            that makes everything commute.
          %p
            In other words,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ev
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev
            define an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/A
            in which taking the product with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the left adjoint and applying this universal property is the right adjoint. This is the basis for the definition below, but we add one further level of generality: We realise that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is secretly
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            is the one-point set (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+object"} final object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            to an arbitrary over category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}/I
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon B \to A
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            along this morphism exist. These then constitute the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            between the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g^* \colon \mathcal{C}_{/A} \to \mathcal{C}_{/B}
                  \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong dependent product
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              is, if it exists, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_g \colon \mathcal{C}_{/B} \to \mathcal{C}_{/A}
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mi g
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi g
                            %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (g^* \dashv \prod_g)
                    \\colon
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/B}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{g^* }{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\prod_g}{\to}}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/A}
                    \\,.
          %p
            So a category with all dependent products is necessarily a category with all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToSpacesOfSections Relation to spaces of sections
          #RelationToSections.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              with all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo *
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/\ast}\cong\mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              be any object and identify it with the terminal morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to *
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/X}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\prod_{x \in X}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{- \times X}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathcal{C}
            %p
              sends
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundles"} bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
              to their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+sections"} object of sections
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi x
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\prod_{x \in X} P_x
                    \\simeq
                    \\Gamma_X(P)
                    \:=
                    [X,P] \times_{[X,X]} \{id\}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We check the characterizing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              for the adjunction: For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
              we have the following sequence of natural isos:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi P
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi 𝒞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mi 𝒞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi p
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi Id
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/X}(A \times X, P \to X)
                    \&amp;=
                    \\mathcal{C}(A \times X, P ) \times_{\mathcal{C}(A \times X, X)} \{p_2\}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\mathcal{C}(A, [X,P]) \times_{\mathcal{C}(A,[X,X])} \{\tilde p_2\}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=
                    \\mathcal{C}(A, [X,P] \times_{[X,X]} \{Id\})
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=  \mathcal{C}(A, \Gamma_X(P))
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This statement and its proof remain valid in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times A
              are cofibrant,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
