          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#in_toposes In toposes
          %p
            Dependent products (and sums) exist in any
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a topos and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to I
              any morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_f : C/A \to C/I
              as well as the right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_f: C/A \to C/I
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*: C/I \to C/A
              exist.
            %p
              Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
              and
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, theorem 2 in section IV, 7
            ).
          %p
            The dependent product plays a role in the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+in+a+topos"} universe in a topos
          %h3#AlongDeloopingsOfGroupHomomorphisms
            Along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}H \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an group object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            (an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            over its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            may be identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-actions"} ∞-actions
            (see there for more):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Act
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Act_G(\mathbf{H}) \simeq \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Under this identification, then dependent product along a morphism of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}H \to \mathbf{B}G
            (corresponding to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            homomorphism
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \to G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinduced+representations"} coinduced representations
          %h3#AlongPointInclusionIntoBG
            Along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            As the special case of the
            %a{:href => "#AlongDeloopingsOfGroupHomomorphisms"} above
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = 1
            the trivial group we obtain the following:
          #GeneralReduction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              be any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a group object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              (an
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \;\colon\; \ast \to \mathbf{B}G
            %p
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              takes the following form:
            %p
              There is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%E2%88%9E-functors"} adjoint ∞-functors
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mi i
                          %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi hofib
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}
                    \\underoverset
                    { \underset{\underset{i}{\prod} \simeq [G,-]/G}{\longrightarrow}}
                    { \overset{i^\ast \simeq hofib}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi hofib
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib
                  denotes the operation of taking the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
                  of a map to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                  over the canonical basepoint;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                  in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]/G
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
                  by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  equipped with its canonical
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
                  by left multiplication and the argument regarded as equipped with its trivial
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed "-action" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %p
                  (for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = S^1
                  then this is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+loop+space"} cyclic loop space
                  construction).
            %p Hence for
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to X
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
                  object, such as for some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            %p
              then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext original
                        %mrow
                          %mtext fluxes
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi oxidation
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi reduction
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext doubly
                        %mrow
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mtext dimensionally reduced
                            %mrow
                              %mtext fluxes
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{original} \atop \text{fluxes}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\mathbf{H}(\hat X\;,\; A)
                    }
                    }
                    \\;\;
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{oxidation}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{reduction}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\simeq}
                    \\;\;
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{doubly} \atop { \text{dimensionally reduced} \atop \text{fluxes} }
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\mathbf{H}(X \;,\; [G,A]/G)
                    }
                    }
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi A
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi G
                              %mo ,
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi G
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\hat X \longrightarrow A
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\leftrightarrow
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; [G,A]/G
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                    }
                    \\right)
          #DimensionalReductionAbstractly.proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The statement that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi hofib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast \simeq hofib
              follows immediately by the definitions. What we need to show is that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is given as claimed.
            %p
              To that end, first observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation action
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,X]
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-actions"} ∞-actions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Act
                        %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Act_G(\mathbf{H})
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Act
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Act_G(\mathbf{H}) \simeq \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
            %p
              (from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+-+fundamental+super+p-branes#NSS12"} NSS 12
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with its canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ast \to \mathbf{B}G)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the trivial action is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \times \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}G)
            %p Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [G,X]/G
                    \\simeq
                    [\ast, X \times \mathbf{B}G]_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\in
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\,.
            %p
              So far this is the very definition of what
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,X]/G \in \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
              is to mean in the first place.
            %p
              But now since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
              is itself
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} cartesian closed
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \times_{\mathbf{B}G}(-)
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\dashv
                    \\;\;\;
                    [E,-]_{\mathbf{B}G}
            %p
              it is immediate that there is the following sequence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalences"} natural equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi G
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ×
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi B
                                  %mi G
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo *
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo !
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi Y
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mrow
                                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                        %mi B
                                      %mi G
                                  %mo *
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mrow
                                %mi hofib
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi hofib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}(Y, [G,X]/G)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}(Y, [\ast, X \times \mathbf{B}G]_{\mathbf{B}G})
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}(
                    Y \times_{\mathbf{B}G} \ast,
                    \\underset{p^\ast X}{\underbrace{X \times \mathbf{B}G }}
                    )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\mathbf{H}(
                    \\underset{hofib(Y)}{\underbrace{p_!(Y \times_{\mathbf{B}G} \ast)}},
                    X
                    )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    \\mathbf{H}(hofib(Y),X)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathbf{B}G \to \ast
              denotes the terminal morphism and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! \dashv p^\ast
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              along it.
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            for more on this.
          %h3#along__3
            Along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
